1
00:06:21,818 --> 00:06:27,818
For justice. For pride. For freedom.

2
00:12:43,636 --> 00:12:49,636
Free State of Jones is a action, drama, history film directed by Gary Ross.

3
00:19:05,454 --> 00:19:11,454
In 1863, Mississippi farmer Newt Knight serves as
a medic for the Confederate Army.

4
00:25:27,272 --> 00:25:33,272
Opposed to slavery, Knight would rather help the wounded than fight the Union.

5
00:31:49,090 --> 00:31:55,090
After his nephew dies in battle, Newt returns home to Jones County to
safeguard his family but is soon branded an outlaw deserter.

6
00:38:10,909 --> 00:38:16,909
Forced to flee, he finds refuge with a group of
runaway slaves hiding out in the swamps.

7
00:44:32,727 --> 00:44:38,727
Forging an alliance with the slaves and other farmers, Knight
leads a rebellion that would forever change history.

8
00:50:54,545 --> 00:51:00,545
Newton Knight, played by Matthew McConaughey.

9
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
Rachel, played by Gugu Mbatha-Raw.

10
01:03:38,181 --> 01:03:44,181
Moses Washington, played by Mahershala Ali.

11
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
Serena Knight, played by Keri Russell.

12
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
Daniel, played by Jacob Lofland.

13
01:22:43,636 --> 01:22:49,636
Sumrall, played by Sean Bridgers.

14
01:29:05,454 --> 01:29:11,454
Free State of Jones is a 2016 American historical war film inspired by the life of Southern Unionist Newton Knight, who led a
successful armed revolt against the Confederacy in Jones County, Mississippi, throughout the American Civil War.

15
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
Written, co-produced, and directed by Gary Ross based on a story by Ross and Leonard Hartman, the
film stars Matthew McConaughey, Gugu Mbatha-Raw, Mahershala Ali, and Keri Russell.

16
01:41:49,090 --> 01:41:55,090
The story is based on the history of Jones County, Mississippi,
during the Civil War and the period immediately after it.

17
01:48:10,909 --> 01:48:16,909
The overall story follows the history of Jones County;
some of the events portrayed are true.

18
01:54:32,727 --> 01:54:38,727
The film is credited as being "based on the books The
Free State of Jones by Victoria E.

19
02:00:54,545 --> 02:01:00,545
Bynum and The State of Jones by Sally Jenkins and John Stauffer."
It was
released in the United States by STXfilms on June 24, 2016.

20
02:07:16,363 --> 02:07:22,363
It received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $25
million against its $50 million production budget.

